</header>

<main class="content">

  <!-- SECTION 1: LCOE TRENDS WITH CROSSOVER -->
  <div class="section-block">
    <div class="section-label">Cost Trajectories</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">LCOE Decline &amp; Fossil Fuel Crossover Points</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">Levelized cost of energy (2023 USD/MWh) for utility-scale solar PV, onshore wind, and battery storage versus the new-build cost range of gas CCGT and coal generation. Crossover annotations mark the years when renewables became cheaper than new fossil capacity.</p>

    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat-callout stat-callout--solar">
        <div class="num">$33<span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:300">/MWh</span></div>
        <div class="pct">↓ 91% since 2010</div>
        <div class="label">Solar PV LCOE 2024</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-callout stat-callout--wind">
        <div class="num">$35<span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:300">/MWh</span></div>
